# Credentials and cluster access — NEVER commit. This repo deploys into real environments and
# every value it needs is a REFERENCE resolved in-cluster by the secrets operator, so anything
# matched below is by definition something that should not exist here at all. A secret that
# reached a remote branch is compromised even after a force-push; gitleaks runs as a
# pre-commit hook and again in CI because "just for a minute" is how it happens.
*.kubeconfig
kubeconfig*
.e2e-kubeconfig
.env
*.key
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx
*.crt
!ca-bundle.crt
secrets.*
vault-token

# Rendered output. Never committed: the bundle is the source, the render is derived, and a
# stale committed render is a second source of truth that reviews perfectly well.
rendered/
*.rendered.yaml

# Python — scripts/ are standalone executables, but they still leave these behind.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/

# Editors / OS
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
